wifi: mt76: mt7925: dump the caller stack on MCU timeout

The command ID alone does not identify which BSS update path timed out.
Dump the stack only on a real timeout so recurring MT7927 firmware hangs
can be tied to the initiating mac80211 operation without continuous
debug logging.

--- a/mt7925/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7925/mcu.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ int mt7925_mcu_parse_response(struct mt76_dev *mdev, int cmd,
 	if (!skb) {
 		dev_err(mdev->dev, "Message %08x (seq %d) timeout\n", cmd, seq);
+		dump_stack();
 		mt792x_reset(mdev);
 
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
